## 2.3  Preparation of MOF/rGO Aerogels
The $\mathbf{MOF/rGO}$ aerogels were synthesized as follows. Typically, $1\mathrm{mL}$ of $10\mathrm{{mg}\mathrm{{mL^{-1}}}}$ MIL-88A aqueous solution was dispersed into $2\mathrm{mL}$ dispersion of GO $\mathrm{5\mg\mL^{-1}},$ ) by shaking for $1~\mathrm{min}$ , standing for 1 min and repeating 3 times, respectively. The solutions were then heated at $95~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for $5\mathrm{h}$ in an oven to form hydrogels. At last, the hydrogels were frozen for $24\mathrm{~h~}$ and freeze-dried for $24\mathrm{~h~}$ to obtain MIL$88\mathrm{A}I$ graphene aerogels. Other Ni-doped MIL-88A/graphene aerogels were synthesized by the same way.
